1
00:00:00,288 --> 00:00:04,916
Balloon Mitral Valvotomy, explained
by Dr. Mohd Maqbool Sohil,

2
00:00:04,966 --> 00:00:06,788
Interventional Cardiologist.

3
00:00:07,208 --> 00:00:09,243
In rheumatic mitral stenosis,

4
00:00:09,339 --> 00:00:13,027
the mitral valve is thickened
and its opening is narrowed,

5
00:00:13,077 --> 00:00:16,565
so blood backs up into
an enlarged left atrium.

6
00:00:17,134 --> 00:00:18,836
This causes breathlessness,

7
00:00:18,896 --> 00:00:23,860
and the enlarged atrium can beat
irregularly, called atrial fibrillation.

8
00:00:24,288 --> 00:00:27,250
The edges of the two
leaflets, the commissures,

9
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:30,359
are fused, leaving a
small fish-mouth opening.

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,178
A normal valve area is 4–6 cm²;
severe stenosis is 1.5 cm² or less.

11
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:40,430
Echo decides suitability.

12
00:00:41,071 --> 00:00:43,821
A transoesophageal echo, or TOE,

13
00:00:43,952 --> 00:00:48,571
checks for clot in the left atrium
and for leakage before the procedure.

14
00:00:49,214 --> 00:00:53,071
A clot or more than mild
leakage usually rules it out.

15
00:00:53,554 --> 00:00:55,814
It is done through a vein in the groin,

16
00:00:55,864 --> 00:00:59,388
without open-heart surgery,
and with no chest cut.

17
00:00:59,992 --> 00:01:02,611
Under local anaesthetic, a needle,

18
00:01:02,707 --> 00:01:06,588
a guidewire and a sheath enter
the femoral vein in the groin.

19
00:01:07,147 --> 00:01:11,195
The route runs up the inferior
vena cava to the right atrium.

20
00:01:11,601 --> 00:01:13,875
Step one: transseptal puncture.

21
00:01:14,539 --> 00:01:18,418
A needle inside a long sheath
crosses the thin fossa ovalis,

22
00:01:18,468 --> 00:01:23,134
in the wall between the atria, from
the right atrium into the left atrium.

23
00:01:23,706 --> 00:01:25,991
Heparin is given to prevent clots.

24
00:01:26,401 --> 00:01:27,210
Step two.

25
00:01:27,863 --> 00:01:33,182
A coiled wire is placed in the left atrium,
the opening in the septum is widened,

26
00:01:33,232 --> 00:01:36,160
and the slender Inoue
balloon follows the wire.

27
00:01:36,601 --> 00:01:37,541
Step three.

28
00:01:38,122 --> 00:01:40,265
With its tip partly inflated,

29
00:01:40,384 --> 00:01:45,301
the balloon is steered across the narrowed
mitral valve into the left ventricle.

30
00:01:45,668 --> 00:01:48,132
Step four: stepwise inflation.

31
00:01:48,737 --> 00:01:52,832
The distal part is inflated and
pulled back against the valve.

32
00:01:53,391 --> 00:01:57,249
The proximal part then
inflates, forming an hourglass.

33
00:01:57,832 --> 00:02:01,320
As the waist expands, the
fused commissures split.

34
00:02:01,768 --> 00:02:02,720
Step five.

35
00:02:03,277 --> 00:02:05,801
The balloon size is based on height.

36
00:02:06,408 --> 00:02:12,108
Inflation starts below the reference size
and is increased one millimetre at a time,

37
00:02:12,158 --> 00:02:15,634
with echo and pressure
checks after each inflation.

38
00:02:16,054 --> 00:02:20,340
After a successful procedure,
the valve opening is larger,

39
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:23,816
and the pressures in the
left atrium and lungs fall.

40
00:02:24,350 --> 00:02:32,016
In one randomised trial, the average
valve area rose from 0.9 to 2.1 cm².

41
00:02:32,588 --> 00:02:35,147
Results vary from person to person.

42
00:02:35,534 --> 00:02:38,558
The sheath is removed from
the vein in the groin.

43
00:02:39,103 --> 00:02:40,937
There is no chest scar.

44
00:02:41,556 --> 00:02:46,199
Many people go home within one to
two days; individual cases vary.

45
00:02:46,782 --> 00:02:48,663
Regular echo check-ups follow.

46
00:02:49,121 --> 00:02:51,952
Major cardiology guidelines
recommend balloon

47
00:02:52,002 --> 00:02:55,071
valvotomy for suitable
patients with symptoms,

48
00:02:55,121 --> 00:02:59,859
and randomised trials found results
comparable to open-heart commissurotomy.

49
00:03:01,121 --> 00:03:04,597
As with any heart
procedure, there are risks,

50
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:08,895
such as valve leakage, bleeding
around the heart, or stroke.

51
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:14,797
Careful selection, imaging and stepwise
inflation are used to reduce them.

52
00:03:15,369 --> 00:03:19,964
Your cardiologist will discuss
benefits and risks for your situation.

53
00:03:20,381 --> 00:03:21,286
Key points.

54
00:03:21,890 --> 00:03:25,259
Through a vein in the groin,
under local anaesthetic,

55
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:28,736
with no open-heart
surgery and no chest cut.

56
00:03:29,367 --> 00:03:32,531
Stepwise inflation splits
the fused commissures,

57
00:03:32,581 --> 00:03:35,759
for a larger valve opening
and lower pressures.

58
00:03:36,188 --> 00:03:41,366
This animation is for education and is
not a substitute for medical advice.

